.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eHow can I upgrade Ollama?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-how-can-i-upgrade-ollama\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: How can I upgrade Ollama?\" href=\"#how-can-i-upgrade-ollama\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eOllama on macOS and Windows will automatically download updates. Click on the taskbar or menubar item and then click \"Restart to update\" to apply the update. Updates can also be installed by downloading the latest version \u003ca href=\"https://ollama.com/download/\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003emanually\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eOn Linux, re-run the install script:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"curl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh\"\u003e\u003cpre class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003ecurl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eHow can I view the logs?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-how-can-i-view-the-logs\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: How can I view the logs?\" href=\"#how-can-i-view-the-logs\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eReview the \u003ca href=\"/ollama/ollama/blob/0b6c6c9092222c850250d8408e7b29056f040bf3/docs/troubleshooting.md\"\u003eTroubleshooting\u003c/a\u003e docs for more about using logs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eHow do I configure Ollama server?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-how-do-i-configure-ollama-server\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: How do I configure Ollama server?\" href=\"#how-do-i-configure-ollama-server\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eOllama server can be configured with environment variables.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch3 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eSetting environment variables on Mac\u003c/h3\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-setting-environment-variables-on-mac\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Setting environment variables on Mac\" href=\"#setting-environment-variables-on-mac\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eIf Ollama is run as a macOS application, environment variables should be set using \u003ccode\u003elaunchctl\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eFor each environment variable, call \u003ccode\u003elaunchctl setenv\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"launchctl setenv OLLAMA_HOST \u0026quot;0.0.0.0\u0026quot;\"\u003e\u003cpre\u003elaunchctl setenv OLLAMA_HOST \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e0.0.0.0\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eRestart Ollama application.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch3 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eSetting environment variables on Linux\u003c/h3\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-setting-environment-variables-on-linux\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Setting environment variables on Linux\" href=\"#setting-environment-variables-on-linux\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eIf Ollama is run as a systemd service, environment variables should be set using \u003ccode\u003esystemctl\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eEdit the systemd service by calling \u003ccode\u003esystemctl edit ollama.service\u003c/code\u003e. This will open an editor.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eFor each environment variable, add a line \u003ccode\u003eEnvironment\u003c/code\u003e under section \u003ccode\u003e[Service]\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-ini notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"[Service]\nEnvironment=\u0026quot;OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0\u0026quot;\"\u003e\u003cpre\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-en\"\u003e[Service]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-k\"\u003eEnvironment\u003c/span\u003e=\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003eOLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eSave and exit.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eReload \u003ccode\u003esystemd\u003c/code\u003e and restart Ollama:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"systemctl daemon-reload\nsystemctl restart ollama\"\u003e\u003cpre\u003esystemctl daemon-reload\nsystemctl restart ollama\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch3 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eSetting environment variables on Windows\u003c/h3\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-setting-environment-variables-on-windows\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Setting environment variables on Windows\" href=\"#setting-environment-variables-on-windows\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eOn windows, Ollama inherits your user and system environment variables.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eFirst Quit Ollama by clicking on it in the task bar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eEdit system environment variables from the control panel\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eEdit or create New variable(s) for your user account for \u003ccode\u003eOLLAMA_HOST\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003eOLLAMA_MODELS\u003c/code\u003e, etc.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eClick OK/Apply to save\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eRun \u003ccode\u003eollama\u003c/code\u003e from a new terminal window\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eHow can I expose Ollama on my network?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-how-can-i-expose-ollama-on-my-network\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: How can I expose Ollama on my network?\" href=\"#how-can-i-expose-ollama-on-my-network\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eOllama binds 127.0.0.1 port 11434 by default. Change the bind address with the \u003ccode\u003eOLLAMA_HOST\u003c/code\u003e environment variable.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eRefer to the section \u003ca href=\"#how-do-i-configure-ollama-server\"\u003eabove\u003c/a\u003e for how to set environment variables on your platform.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eHow can I allow additional web origins to access Ollama?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-how-can-i-allow-additional-web-origins-to-access-ollama\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: How can I allow additional web origins to access Ollama?\" href=\"#how-can-i-allow-additional-web-origins-to-access-ollama\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eOllama allows cross-origin requests from \u003ccode\u003e127.0.0.1\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003e0.0.0.0\u003c/code\u003e by default. Additional origins can be configured with \u003ccode\u003eOLLAMA_ORIGINS\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eRefer to the section \u003ca href=\"#how-do-i-configure-ollama-server\"\u003eabove\u003c/a\u003e for how to set environment variables on your platform.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eWhere are models stored?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-where-are-models-stored\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Where are models stored?\" href=\"#where-are-models-stored\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003emacOS: \u003ccode\u003e~/.ollama/models\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLinux: \u003ccode\u003e/usr/share/ollama/.ollama/models\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWindows: \u003ccode\u003eC:\\Users\\\u0026lt;username\u0026gt;\\.ollama\\models\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch3 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eHow do I set them to a different location?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-how-do-i-set-them-to-a-different-location\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: How do I set them to a different location?\" href=\"#how-do-i-set-them-to-a-different-location\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eIf a different directory needs to be used, set the environment variable \u003ccode\u003eOLLAMA_MODELS\u003c/code\u003e to the chosen directory.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eRefer to the section \u003ca href=\"#how-do-i-configure-ollama-server\"\u003eabove\u003c/a\u003e for how to set environment variables on your platform.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eDoes Ollama send my prompts and answers back to Ollama.ai to use in any way?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-does-ollama-send-my-prompts-and-answers-back-to-ollamaai-to-use-in-any-way\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Does Ollama send my prompts and answers back to Ollama.ai to use in any way?\" href=\"#does-ollama-send-my-prompts-and-answers-back-to-ollamaai-to-use-in-any-way\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eNo, Ollama runs entirely locally, and conversation data will never leave your machine.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eHow can I use Ollama in Visual Studio Code?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-how-can-i-use-ollama-in-visual-studio-code\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: How can I use Ollama in Visual Studio Code?\" href=\"#how-can-i-use-ollama-in-visual-studio-code\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThere is already a large collection of plugins available for VSCode as well as other editors that leverage Ollama. See the list of \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/jmorganca/ollama#extensions--plugins\"\u003eextensions \u0026amp; plugins\u003c/a\u003e at the bottom of the main repository readme.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eHow do I use Ollama behind a proxy?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-how-do-i-use-ollama-behind-a-proxy\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: How do I use Ollama behind a proxy?\" href=\"#how-do-i-use-ollama-behind-a-proxy\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eOllama is compatible with proxy servers if \u003ccode\u003eHTTP_PROXY\u003c/code\u003e or \u003ccode\u003eHTTPS_PROXY\u003c/code\u003e are configured. When using either variables, ensure it is set where \u003ccode\u003eollama serve\u003c/code\u003e can access the values. When using \u003ccode\u003eHTTPS_PROXY\u003c/code\u003e, ensure the proxy certificate is installed as a system certificate. Refer to the section above for how to use environment variables on your platform.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch3 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eHow do I use Ollama behind a proxy in Docker?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-how-do-i-use-ollama-behind-a-proxy-in-docker\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: How do I use Ollama behind a proxy in Docker?\" href=\"#how-do-i-use-ollama-behind-a-proxy-in-docker\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThe Ollama Docker container image can be configured to use a proxy by passing \u003ccode\u003e-e HTTPS_PROXY=https://proxy.example.com\u003c/code\u003e when starting the container.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eAlternatively, the Docker daemon can be configured to use a proxy. Instructions are available for Docker Desktop on \u003ca href=\"https://docs.docker.com/desktop/settings/mac/#proxies\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003emacOS\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href=\"https://docs.docker.com/desktop/settings/windows/#proxies\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003eWindows\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href=\"https://docs.docker.com/desktop/settings/linux/#proxies\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003eLinux\u003c/a\u003e, and Docker \u003ca href=\"https://docs.docker.com/config/daemon/systemd/#httphttps-proxy\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003edaemon with systemd\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eEnsure the certificate is installed as a system certificate when using HTTPS. This may require a new Docker image when using a self-signed certificate.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-dockerfile notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"FROM ollama/ollama\nCOPY my-ca.pem /usr/local/share/ca-certificates/my-ca.crt\nRUN update-ca-certificates\"\u003e\u003cpre\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-k\"\u003eFROM\u003c/span\u003e ollama/ollama\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-k\"\u003eCOPY\u003c/span\u003e my-ca.pem /usr/local/share/ca-certificates/my-ca.crt\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-k\"\u003eRUN\u003c/span\u003e update-ca-certificates\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eBuild and run this image:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"docker build -t ollama-with-ca .\ndocker run -d -e HTTPS_PROXY=https://my.proxy.example.com -p 11434:11434 ollama-with-ca\"\u003e\u003cpre\u003edocker build -t ollama-with-ca \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\ndocker run -d -e HTTPS_PROXY=https://my.proxy.example.com -p 11434:11434 ollama-with-ca\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eHow do I use Ollama with GPU acceleration in Docker?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-how-do-i-use-ollama-with-gpu-acceleration-in-docker\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: How do I use Ollama with GPU acceleration in Docker?\" href=\"#how-do-i-use-ollama-with-gpu-acceleration-in-docker\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThe Ollama Docker container can be configured with GPU acceleration in Linux or Windows (with WSL2). This requires the \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/NVIDIA/nvidia-container-toolkit\"\u003envidia-container-toolkit\u003c/a\u003e. See \u003ca href=\"https://hub.docker.com/r/ollama/ollama\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003eollama/ollama\u003c/a\u003e for more details.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eGPU acceleration is not available for Docker Desktop in macOS due to the lack of GPU passthrough and emulation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eWhy is networking slow in WSL2 on Windows 10?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-why-is-networking-slow-in-wsl2-on-windows-10\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Why is networking slow in WSL2 on Windows 10?\" href=\"#why-is-networking-slow-in-wsl2-on-windows-10\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThis can impact both installing Ollama, as well as downloading models.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eOpen \u003ccode\u003eControl Panel \u0026gt; Networking and Internet \u0026gt; View network status and tasks\u003c/code\u003e and click on \u003ccode\u003eChange adapter settings\u003c/code\u003e on the left panel. Find the \u003ccode\u003evEthernel (WSL)\u003c/code\u003e adapter, right click and select \u003ccode\u003eProperties\u003c/code\u003e.\nClick on \u003ccode\u003eConfigure\u003c/code\u003e and open the \u003ccode\u003eAdvanced\u003c/code\u003e tab. Search through each of the properties until you find \u003ccode\u003eLarge Send Offload Version 2 (IPv4)\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eLarge Send Offload Version 2 (IPv6)\u003c/code\u003e. \u003cem\u003eDisable\u003c/em\u003e both of these\nproperties.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eHow can I pre-load a model to get faster response times?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-how-can-i-pre-load-a-model-to-get-faster-response-times\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: How can I pre-load a model to get faster response times?\" href=\"#how-can-i-pre-load-a-model-to-get-faster-response-times\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eIf you are using the API you can preload a model by sending the Ollama server an empty request. This works with both the \u003ccode\u003e/api/generate\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003e/api/chat\u003c/code\u003e API endpoints.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eTo preload the mistral model using the generate endpoint, use:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"curl http://localhost:11434/api/generate -d '{\u0026quot;model\u0026quot;: \u0026quot;mistral\u0026quot;}'\"\u003e\u003cpre\u003ecurl http://localhost:11434/api/generate -d \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e'\u003c/span\u003e{\"model\": \"mistral\"}\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e'\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eTo use the chat completions endpoint, use:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"curl http://localhost:11434/api/chat -d '{\u0026quot;model\u0026quot;: \u0026quot;mistral\u0026quot;}'\"\u003e\u003cpre\u003ecurl http://localhost:11434/api/chat -d \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e'\u003c/span\u003e{\"model\": \"mistral\"}\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e'\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eHow do I keep a model loaded in memory or make it unload immediately?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-how-do-i-keep-a-model-loaded-in-memory-or-make-it-unload-immediately\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: How do I keep a model loaded in memory or make it unload immediately?\" href=\"#how-do-i-keep-a-model-loaded-in-memory-or-make-it-unload-immediately\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eBy default models are kept in memory for 5 minutes before being unloaded. This allows for quicker response times if you are making numerous requests to the LLM. You may, however, want to free up the memory before the 5 minutes have elapsed or keep the model loaded indefinitely. Use the \u003ccode\u003ekeep_alive\u003c/code\u003e parameter with either the \u003ccode\u003e/api/generate\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003e/api/chat\u003c/code\u003e API endpoints to control how long the model is left in memory.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThe \u003ccode\u003ekeep_alive\u003c/code\u003e parameter can be set to:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ea duration string (such as \"10m\" or \"24h\")\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ea number in seconds (such as 3600)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eany negative number which will keep the model loaded in memory (e.g. -1 or \"-1m\")\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e'0' which will unload the model immediately after generating a response\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eFor example, to preload a model and leave it in memory use:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"curl http://localhost:11434/api/generate -d '{\u0026quot;model\u0026quot;: \u0026quot;llama2\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;keep_alive\u0026quot;: -1}'\"\u003e\u003cpre\u003ecurl http://localhost:11434/api/generate -d \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e'\u003c/span\u003e{\"model\": \"llama2\", \"keep_alive\": -1}\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e'\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eTo unload the model and free up memory use:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"curl http://localhost:11434/api/generate -d '{\u0026quot;model\u0026quot;: \u0026quot;llama2\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;keep_alive\u0026quot;: 0}'\"\u003e\u003cpre\u003ecurl http://localhost:11434/api/generate -d \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e'\u003c/span\u003e{\"model\": \"llama2\", \"keep_alive\": 0}\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e'\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/article\u003e","richTextTruncated":false,"renderedFileInfo":null,"symbols":{"timed_out":false,"not_analyzed":false,"symbols":[{"name":"FAQ","fully_qualified_name":"FAQ","kind":"section_1","ident_start":2,"ident_end":5,"extent_start":0,"extent_end":7373,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":0,"utf16_col":2},"end":{"line_number":0,"utf16_col":5}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":0,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":173,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"How can I upgrade Ollama?","fully_qualified_name":"How can I upgrade Ollama?","kind":"section_2","ident_start":10,"ident_end":35,"extent_start":7,"extent_end":395,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":2,"utf16_col":3},"end":{"line_number":2,"utf16_col":28}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":2,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":12,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"How can I view the logs?","fully_qualified_name":"How can I view the logs?","kind":"section_2","ident_start":398,"ident_end":422,"extent_start":395,"extent_end":508,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":12,"utf16_col":3},"end":{"line_number":12,"utf16_col":27}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":12,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":16,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"How do I configure Ollama server?","fully_qualified_name":"How do I configure Ollama server?","kind":"section_2","ident_start":511,"ident_end":544,"extent_start":508,"extent_end":1841,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":16,"utf16_col":3},"end":{"line_number":16,"utf16_col":36}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":16,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":69,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"Setting environment variables on Mac","fully_qualified_name":"Setting environment variables on Mac","kind":"section_3","ident_start":611,"ident_end":647,"extent_start":607,"extent_end":902,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":20,"utf16_col":4},"end":{"line_number":20,"utf16_col":40}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":20,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":32,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"Setting environment variables on Linux","fully_qualified_name":"Setting environment variables on Linux","kind":"section_3","ident_start":906,"ident_end":944,"extent_start":902,"extent_end":1433,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":32,"utf16_col":4},"end":{"line_number":32,"utf16_col":42}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":32,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":54,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"Setting environment variables on Windows","fully_qualified_name":"Setting environment variables on Windows","kind":"section_3","ident_start":1437,"ident_end":1477,"extent_start":1433,"extent_end":1841,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":54,"utf16_col":4},"end":{"line_number":54,"utf16_col":44}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":54,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":69,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"How can I expose Ollama on my network?","fully_qualified_name":"How can I expose Ollama on my network?","kind":"section_2","ident_start":1844,"ident_end":1882,"extent_start":1841,"extent_end":2120,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":69,"utf16_col":3},"end":{"line_number":69,"utf16_col":41}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":69,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":75,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"How can I allow additional web origins to access Ollama?","fully_qualified_name":"How can I allow additional web origins to access Ollama?","kind":"section_2","ident_start":2123,"ident_end":2179,"extent_start":2120,"extent_end":2441,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":75,"utf16_col":3},"end":{"line_number":75,"utf16_col":59}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":75,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":81,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"Where are models stored?","fully_qualified_name":"Where are models stored?","kind":"section_2","ident_start":2444,"ident_end":2468,"extent_start":2441,"extent_end":2873,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":81,"utf16_col":3},"end":{"line_number":81,"utf16_col":27}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":81,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":93,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"How do I set them to a different location?","fully_qualified_name":"How do I set them to a different location?","kind":"section_3","ident_start":2595,"ident_end":2637,"extent_start":2591,"extent_end":2873,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":87,"utf16_col":4},"end":{"line_number":87,"utf16_col":46}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":87,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":93,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"Does Ollama send my prompts and answers back to Ollama.ai to use in any way?","fully_qualified_name":"Does Ollama send my prompts and answers back to Ollama.ai to use in any way?","kind":"section_2","ident_start":2876,"ident_end":2952,"extent_start":2873,"extent_end":3042,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":93,"utf16_col":3},"end":{"line_number":93,"utf16_col":79}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":93,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":97,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"How can I use Ollama in Visual Studio Code?","fully_qualified_name":"How can I use Ollama in Visual Studio Code?","kind":"section_2","ident_start":3045,"ident_end":3088,"extent_start":3042,"extent_end":3347,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":97,"utf16_col":3},"end":{"line_number":97,"utf16_col":46}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":97,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":101,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"How do I use Ollama behind a proxy?","fully_qualified_name":"How do I use Ollama behind a proxy?","kind":"section_2","ident_start":3350,"ident_end":3385,"extent_start":3347,"extent_end":4801,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":101,"utf16_col":3},"end":{"line_number":101,"utf16_col":38}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":101,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":126,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"How do I use Ollama behind a proxy in Docker?","fully_qualified_name":"How do I use Ollama behind a proxy in Docker?","kind":"section_3","ident_start":3746,"ident_end":3791,"extent_start":3742,"extent_end":4801,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":105,"utf16_col":4},"end":{"line_number":105,"utf16_col":49}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":105,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":126,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"How do I use Ollama with GPU acceleration in Docker?","fully_qualified_name":"How do I use Ollama with GPU acceleration in Docker?","kind":"section_2","ident_start":4804,"ident_end":4856,"extent_start":4801,"extent_end":5249,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":126,"utf16_col":3},"end":{"line_number":126,"utf16_col":55}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":126,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":132,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"Why is networking slow in WSL2 on Windows 10?","fully_qualified_name":"Why is networking slow in WSL2 on Windows 10?","kind":"section_2","ident_start":5252,"ident_end":5297,"extent_start":5249,"extent_end":5802,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":132,"utf16_col":3},"end":{"line_number":132,"utf16_col":48}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":132,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":140,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"How can I pre-load a model to get faster response times?","fully_qualified_name":"How can I pre-load a model to get faster response times?","kind":"section_2","ident_start":5805,"ident_end":5861,"extent_start":5802,"extent_end":6296,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":140,"utf16_col":3},"end":{"line_number":140,"utf16_col":59}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":140,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":154,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"How do I keep a model loaded in memory or make it unload immediately?","fully_qualified_name":"How do I keep a model loaded in memory or make it unload immediately?","kind":"section_2","ident_start":6299,"ident_end":6368,"extent_start":6296,"extent_end":7373,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":154,"utf16_col":3},"end":{"line_number":154,"utf16_col":72}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":154,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":173,"utf16_col":0}}}]}},"codeViewLayoutRoute":{"repo":{"id":658928958,"defaultBranch":"main","name":"ollama","ownerLogin":"ollama","currentUserCanPush":false,"isFork":false,"isEmpty":false,"createdAt":"2023-06-26T19:39:32.000Z","ownerAvatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151674099?v=4","public":true,"private":false,"isOrgOwned":true,"isArchived":false},"currentUser":null,"uploadToken":"jBtpKsmLwELxrpwIhxqL6fAUsB1yU6xsWKDjZuy3BJw1CpY6prP6MhOBa2Z80w3qYItEo8gWrukDaqW4hTKQww","allShortcutsEnabled":false,"treeExpanded":true,"path":"docs/faq.md","symbolsExpanded":false,"refInfo":{"name":"0b6c6c9092222c850250d8408e7b29056f040bf3","listCacheKey":"v0:1792857108.0","canEdit":false,"currentOid":"0b6c6c9092222c850250d8408e7b29056f040bf3"},"helpUrl":"https://docs.github.com","githubDevUrl":null},"codeViewFileTreeLayoutRoute":{"fileTree":{"docs":{"items":[{"name":"tutorials","path":"docs/tutorials","contentType":"directory"},{"name":"README.md","path":"docs/README.md","contentType":"file"},{"name":"api.md","path":"docs/api.md","contentType":"file"},{"name":"development.md","path":"docs/development.md","contentType":"file"},{"name":"faq.md","path":"docs/faq.md","contentType":"file"},{"name":"import.md","path":"docs/import.md","contentType":"file"},{"name":"linux.md","path":"docs/linux.md","contentType":"file"},{"name":"modelfile.md","path":"docs/modelfile.md","contentType":"file"},{"name":"openai.md","path":"docs/openai.md","contentType":"file"},{"name":"troubleshooting.md","path":"docs/troubleshooting.md","contentType":"file"},{"name":"tutorials.md","path":"docs/tutorials.md","contentType":"file"},{"name":"windows.md","path":"docs/windows.md","contentType":"file"}],"totalCount":12},"":{"items":[{"name":".github","path":".github","contentType":"directory"},{"name":"api","path":"api","contentType":"directory"},{"name":"ap